  "notes": "Godan verb (む row: {励|はげ}む → {励|はげ}まない → {励|はげ}んで). Takes the pattern ～に{励|はげ}む (to devote oneself to ~). The activity one works on is marked with に.\n\nNot to be confused with the transitive form {励|はげ}ます (to encourage someone).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {勉強|べんきょう}に{励|はげ}む — to devote oneself to study\n- {仕事|しごと}に{励|はげ}む — to work hard at one's job\n- {練習|れんしゅう}に{励|はげ}む — to work hard at practice\n- {研究|けんきゅう}に{励|はげ}む — to devote oneself to research",
